abstract: >
  GlyVAS (Glycan Validated Abundances from Spectra;
  formerly LC-MS Data Processor) is open-source Python
  software that quantifies labeled glycans from mzML
  files over a grid of processing settings, compares the
  result with the fluorescence trace from the same
  injection and with Skyline, and fits per-glycan
  response factors that are tested on runs not used to
  fit them. Its target calculator covers N- and
  O-glycans, milk oligosaccharides and glycosaminoglycan
  disaccharides. It also provides general chromatogram
  processing: baseline, peak detection and integration,
  signal-to-noise, peak shape, resolution and linear
  calibration.
